T17:00:35Z","completedAt":"2026-07-19T17:02:29Z"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","name":"build","status":"COMPLETED","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit/actions/runs/29695976183/job/88216694470","startedAt":"2026-07-19T17:00:34Z","completedAt":"2026-07-19T17:01:47Z"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","name":"check-codebase","status":"COMPLETED","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit/actions/runs/29695976183/job/88216694486","startedAt":"2026-07-19T17:00:34Z","completedAt":"2026-07-19T17:01:01Z"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","name":"lint","status":"COMPLETED","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit/actions/runs/29695976183/job/88216694477","startedAt":"2026-07-19T17:00:34Z","completedAt":"2026-07-19T17:01:24Z"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","name":"check-for-fixups","status":"COMPLETED","conclusion":"FAILURE","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit/actions/runs/29695976183/job/88216694527","startedAt":"2026-07-19T17:00:34Z","completedAt":"2026-07-19T17:00:41Z"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","name":"upload-coverage","status":"COMPLETED","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit/actions/runs/29695976183/job/88216869439","startedAt":"2026-07-19T17:02:30Z","completedAt":"2026-07-19T17:02:30Z"}]}}}}]},"comments":{"pageInfo":{"hasNextPage":false,"endCursor":"Y3Vyc29yOnYyOpHPAAAAASFNE_I="},"nodes":[{"id":"IC_kwDOB_zxBs8AAAABHukmxg","author":{"login":"scottchiefbaker"},"body":"I'm about 8 minutes into your demo video and I'm already very excited. Conceptually it seems simple enough. I just need to add some \"hidden\" escape codes into the d-s-f output to mark changed lines?","createdAt":"2026-06-26T21:28:25Z","url":"https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit/pull/5732#issuecomment-4813563590"},{"id":"IC_kwDOB_zxBs8AAAABHutQZA","author":{"login":"scottchiefbaker"},"body":"9. Where feedback is most wanted\r\n\r\n> 1. The OSC number, 1717....\r\n\r\nI don't know enough about OSC codes to have a strong opinion on this. But 1717 seems fine to me.\r\n\r\n> 2. The env-var name and grammar (EMIT_OSC1717_METADATA=V1,…).\r\n\r\nThis seems fine to me I think.\r\n\r\n> 3. The token-vs-line mismatch (§8) — should there be an m type, or is host-side inference the right home for it?\r\n\r\nNot sure I have enough information to say on this.\r\n\r\n> 4. Can your pager actually produce all four fields per region?\r\n\r\nI believe so. I'd definitely like to work closer with you to beta-test this feature as there are a lot of technical details I don't 100% follow quite yet.\r\n\r\n> 5. Content-lines-only scope (§5.5) — is anything lost for your pager?\r\n\r\nI don't think so. d-s-f parses line by line, and retains header information so I should be able to call back to the last header when I encounter a line change.","createdAt":"2026-06-26T21:57:33Z","url":"https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit/pull/5732#issuecomment-4813705316"},{"id":"IC_kwDOB_zxBs8AAAABHuzOYw","author":{"login":"scottchiefbaker"},"body":"Having read the [spec document](https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit/blob/e6acab85ad8969112bb514b7d5c49e06e5073775/diff-line-metadata-osc-spec.md) and watched your video can I get clarification on a couple of things?\r\n\r\n1. In this new metadata mode `lazygit` (or whoever) emits an environment variable `EMIT_OSC1717_METADATA = V1[,V2,…]` when it's in select hunk/line mode.\r\n2. If a pager sees this environment variable it needs to output a \"handshake\" as the first part of it's output indicating what version of OSC1717 it understands? `\"\\e]1717;1\\e\\\"`\r\n3. Will each line of context (the lines that are NOT changing) need a OSC1717 record? In the case of d-s-f which does line-by-line output, **every** output line will have a record?\r\n4. From section 6.1 \"One record per region, at the region's start\". In this hypothetical diff which contains: a line add, a line change, and a li ne delete, how many \"regions\" would that be? 3? 4? Or is region another way of saying \"line\" in which case there would be 20?\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/LICENSE b/LICENSE\r\nindex eb26539..028c6af 100644\r\n--- a/LICENSE\r\n+++ b/LICENSE\r\n@@ -5,17 +5,18 @@ Copyright (c) 2016 So Fancy team\r\n Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\r\n of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\r\n in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\r\n-to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\r\n copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\r\n furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\r\n\r\n The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in\r\n all copies or substantial portions of the Software.\r\n\r\n+FOOBAR\r\n THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\r\n IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\r\n FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\r\n AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\r\n-LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\r\n+LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM;\r\n OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN\r\n THE SOFTWARE.\r\n```\r\n\r\nHelp me understand the fields for the deleted line. Would it be: `\"\\e]1717;1;d;;8;b/LICENSE\\e\\\"`? I don't fully understand old line vs new line.\r\n\r\nFor the added line. Would it be: `\"\\e]1717;1;a;15;;b/LICENSE\\e\\\"`?\r\n\r\nIn section 4.3 it says \"context, new line 10\" but I think it would be more clear as \"context, line 10\" because it's not new.","createdAt":"2026-06-26T22:18:48Z","url":"https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit/pull/5732#issuecomment-4813803107"},{"id":"IC_kwDOB_zxBs8AAAABHvDGoA","author":{"login":"scottchiefbaker"},"body":"Possible minor hiccup? While attempting to implement the basics of this I came across a minor problem:\r\n\r\n```\r\n# Works fine\r\nperl -E 'print \"\\e]1717;1\\e\\\\\"'\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n# Outputs `\\`\r\nperl -E 'print \"\\e]1717;1\\e\\\\\"' | less\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe default mode with d-s-f it to pipe through less as a pager, and it appears `less` doesn't handle OSC escape sequences super cleanly.","createdAt":"2026-06-26T23:22:44Z","url":"https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit/pull/5732#issuecomment-4814063264"},{"id":"IC_kwDOB_zxBs8AAAABHwSD3w","author":{"login":"stefanhaller"},"body":"> While attempting to implement the basics of this ...\r\n\r\nI must not have made that clear enough: you don't have to do that, I did already. I just didn't post a (draft) PR yet because I first wanted to get feedback on the spec; but the changes are ready (apart from the necessary changes to the docs, if any, and to the changelog etc.). My branch is [here](https://github.com/so-fancy/diff-so-fancy/compare/next...stefanhaller:diff-so-fancy:prototype-osc-metadata) if you want to try it.\r\n\r\n> it appears `less` doesn't handle OSC escape sequences super cleanly.\r\n\r\nThat's too bad, but it's not a problem, because d-s-f will only emit the sequences when it is running inside lazygit.\r\n\r\nI'm taking your other questions over to #5731, that's where the spec should be discussed.","createdAt":"2026-06-27T05:14:49Z","url":"https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit/pull/5732#issuecomment-4815356895"},{"id":"IC_kwDOB_zxBs8AAAABH0z1eg","author":{"login":"scottchiefbaker"},"body":"Oh man... you didn't tell me you had most of the work done in d-s-f. You should have led with that. Your code looks pretty sane to me. Well done.","createdAt":"2026-06-27T18:27:42Z","url":"https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit/pull/5732#issuecomment-4820104570"},{"id":"IC_kwDOB_zxBs8AAAABIQYKiA","author":{"login":"nullromo"},"body":"Just want to say that this prototype looks very exciting and I would be ecstatic if these changes landed in an official Lazygit release.","createdAt":"2026-07-01T00:11:10Z","url":"https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit/pull/5732#issuecomment-4849011336"},{"id":"IC_kwDOB_zxBs8AAAABIU0T8g","author":{"login":"jesseduffield"},"body":"This looks amazing. This would be a serious game-changer for my workflow and I imagine many others as well.","createdAt":"2026-07-01T11:05:00Z","url":"https://github.com/jesseduffield/lazygit/pull/5732#issuecomment-4853666802"}]}}}}}